WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.283 --> 00:00:02.661
- I don't know anything about cricket.

00:00:02.661 --> 00:00:04.705
- There's no real crickets in it.

00:00:04.705 --> 00:00:09.570
("Four Seasons - Spring")

00:00:22.264 --> 00:00:23.640
- The bat is called a wicket.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.601
- The wicket's the ball I believe.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:26.852
- When I think about cricket I think about

00:00:26.852 --> 00:00:28.312
the outfits that they're wearing.

00:00:28.312 --> 00:00:31.148
Shorts and like a jacket or
something. It seems very proper.

00:00:31.148 --> 00:00:33.108
- So I guess there's a lot of different

00:00:33.108 --> 00:00:36.528
accessories for your cricket outfit.

00:00:36.528 --> 00:00:38.989
The entire time that we have
been talking about cricket

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.089
I've been envisioning croquet.

00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:46.288
- It's like squash had
a baby with baseball.

00:00:46.288 --> 00:00:48.415
- So green is Pakistan, blue is India.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.542
- There's someone wearing blue,
there's someone wearing red

00:00:50.542 --> 00:00:52.132
and there's someone wearing black

00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:54.129
and I think only two teams playing.

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:56.423
- There's a cowboy on the field.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.799
- Is that a Mountie?

00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:58.967
- That must be the ref.

00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:00.635
- He looks like a Canadian Mountie.

00:01:00.635 --> 00:01:03.021
- He's definitely not called
an umpire, I know that.

00:01:05.766 --> 00:01:08.685
- Home run! I think.

00:01:08.685 --> 00:01:10.228
- What are the bars in the middle?

00:01:10.228 --> 00:01:11.814
- That's a sign.

00:01:11.814 --> 00:01:13.815
That's a sign. This means something.

00:01:13.815 --> 00:01:16.026
- I'm not really sure where the bases are.

00:01:16.026 --> 00:01:19.112
Still have no clue how
they acquire points.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.822
- It's like there are no outfielders.

00:01:20.822 --> 00:01:23.992
So maybe the goal is
not to catch the ball.

00:01:23.992 --> 00:01:26.620
- He's trying to hit the
ball along the ground.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.746
Well then, why were they so excited

00:01:27.746 --> 00:01:29.331
before when they went far away?

00:01:29.331 --> 00:01:30.957
- I have no idea what's going on here.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.542
This is very confusing.

00:01:32.542 --> 00:01:34.712
- Where are they trying to get the ball?

00:01:34.712 --> 00:01:36.087
It feels like it can go anywhere.

00:01:36.087 --> 00:01:37.339
- He said that was a lovely shot.

00:01:37.339 --> 00:01:39.424
It rolled towards a line

00:01:39.424 --> 00:01:41.718
that looked like a
warning track in baseball.

00:01:44.555 --> 00:01:46.264
- I know less now about cricket

00:01:46.264 --> 00:01:47.974
than I knew before we watched it.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:48.683
- I think it looks dope.

00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:50.519
- I don't even know how
many rounds there are.

00:01:50.519 --> 00:01:51.937
Like how many points you need to win.

00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:53.339
- We didn't even know
what they were doing.

00:01:53.339 --> 00:01:56.399
- I'm definitely not going
to look out for it on ESPN.

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:58.318
- Any sport with cowboys
could probably easily

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.995
become second nature to me eventually.

